Talk about an irritating bug.  I just recently picked up the CD-ROM 
edition of Ultima Underworld I & II.  After installing, I began the 
character generation sequence on I, which would bomb as soon as I began 
typing the character name.  I had sufficient memory on my system, so after 
several attempts to create a character, I reinstalled the game.  
Nevertheless, the program still bombed.  After a suggestion by my son, we 
found out what the problem is:  using the shift key to capitalize a 
letter bombs the program!  Even odder, using Caps Lock does not!  This 
may not seem like much in a mouse-driven game, but whenever you save a 
game, you are in danger of accidentally trying to capitalize the name of 
your save file, which will then bomb the program without saving.  I don't 
know if this problem occured on the floppy versions, nor whether it 
occurs in Underworld II on the CD ROM, but one version with this bug is 
annoying enough.  Does the customer service number include a bug report 
option?  I'd love to gently smack them around verbally.


